        {
          "path": "_m/g/c/v/2/sweetheart-abbey-wp/plaque-in-memory-of-william-pa.jpg",
          "filename": "Plaque in memory of William Paterson - geograph.org.uk - 1156837.jpg",
          "caption": "Plaque in memory of William Paterson This plaque on the wall surrounding Sweetheart Abbey is to William Paterson(1658 - 1719), the founder of the Bank of England. He was born at Skipnayre farm near Lochmaben and it is thought may be buried here. After several years trading in the West Indies he founded the Bank of England in 1694. He also promoted the Darien Scheme,Scotland's disastrous attempt to establish a colony at Panama sailing there with the first party but returned in 1699. A supporter of the Union he was MP in the first united parliament.",
          "alt": "Plaque in memory of William Paterson This plaque on the wall surrounding Sweetheart Abbey is to William Paterson(1658 - 1719), the founder of the Bank of England. He was born at Skipnayre farm near Lochmaben and it is thought may be buried here. After several years trading in the West Indies he founded the Bank of England in 1694. He also promoted the Darien Scheme,Scotland's disastrous attempt to establish a colony at Panama sailing there with the first party but returned in 1699. A supporter of the Union he was MP in the first united parliament.",
          "width": 640,
          "height": 415,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
          "artist": "ronnie leask",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Plaque_in_memory_of_William_Paterson_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1156837.jpg",
